From a8f75b08bcc3d233a667106f7bfc76759dc07902 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wadood <wc2595@columbia.edu>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:39:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Positioned runtime: filter plain selection formulas in SQL,
 split formula and SQL parameters, bind subreport queries by identifier
 (0.1.116)

A host's PO formats are positioned Crystal designs whose record selection is
{POMaster.PONumber} = {?PONumber} AND {POMaster.DivisionID} = {?DivisionID}.
The positioned loader built every query with an empty where clause, so a
preview read the whole table against GuardRowLimit and the multi-value
parameter never reached SQL. RefreshSql now passes a plain AND/OR of field,
parameter and literal comparisons as the where clause (a multi-value
parameter only behind "= {?P}", which the IN rewrite expands); any other
formula keeps the runtime evaluation. Only this report's tables are
projected: an SDK export lists a link's main field among the subreport's
fields, and a parameter is read from the values, not the query.

ReportWriterControl's positioned branch keeps the formula parameters (a
multi-value selection as string[]) apart from the rewritten SQL parameters.
Subreport queries bind by SQL identifier, one value as itself, several as
IN on a copy of the child definition; a "{?Pm-X}" link name is stored bare.
SDK-export object kinds map to the designer vocabulary.

ReportDesigner.RuntimeTests 568, CrystalSemanticsTests 85, HomeFront
ReportManagerChecks 97. FlexCore port pending (checkout on another branch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
